@startuml arch_pibt
title Architecture detail C — PIBT algorithm (simulation/algo/pibt.py)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam ClassBorderColor #555555

abstract class Coordinator {
    + {abstract} plan(agents:list[Agent], grid:Grid) : dict[int,Position]
}

class PIBT {
    + goals : dict[Agent,Position]
    + priorities : dict[Agent,float]
    - _next : dict[Agent,Position]
    - _processed : set[Agent]
    - _grid : Grid | None
    + _last_order : list[Agent]
    + _last_moves : dict[Agent,(Position,Position)]
    + _last_inheritance : list[(Agent,Agent)]
    --
    + plan(agents:list[Agent], grid:Grid) : dict[int,Position]
    - _pibt(agent:Agent, parent:Agent|None) : bool
    - _h(pos:Position, agent:Agent) : int
    - _reserving_agent(pos:Position) : Agent | None
    - _init_priorities_if_needed(agents)
    .. constants ..
    DIRS = 4-neighbour    EPSILON = 1e-3
}

PIBT .up.|> Coordinator

note right of PIBT
  plan() — one coordinated pass:
   1. priorities -= 1 for all
   2. agent at its goal -> priority = -inf
   3. order = agents sorted by priority desc
   4. for each unprocessed agent: _pibt(agent, None)
   5. return {agent_id -> next Position}

  _pibt(agent, parent) — Algorithm 1 (Okumura et al. 2022):
   • candidates = free 4-neighbours, sorted by Manhattan _h to goal
   • agent already at goal -> prefer staying in place
   • skip the parent's cell (no swap back)
   • reserve a free candidate in _next
   • if candidate holds an occupant NOT yet planned:
       occupant inherits priority (+EPSILON) and _pibt(occupant, agent)  [priority inheritance]
       success -> keep; failure -> release and try next candidate     [backtracking]
   • no candidate works -> stay put, return False

  tracking (_last_*) is read by the Level 0 viewer to draw order / moves / inheritance chains
end note

@enduml
